{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["<b>Take for yourself.</b> Take him with words — fortunate are you that you merited to lead the children of the Omnipresent." "<b>For yourself.</b> That which is known to you, that which you recognize." "<b>In whom is spirit.</b> As you asked — that he can go against the spirit of each and every one (Sifrei)." "<b>And lay your hand upon him.</b> Give him a spokesman who shall teach in your lifetime, so that they not say of him: he had no standing to lift his head in the days of Moses."], :book :numbers, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:13:02.969319959Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}